# Plain language

Write documents so a teammate can follow them on one read. This covers ADRs, PRDs, PR descriptions, tickets, design notes, and review comments.

Use the technical term when it is the precise name: an API, an IAM role, a story point, a specific file. Do not replace that term with a vague phrase.

Say what is true and what to do. Use short sentences. Name the thing, then say what happens to it.

Leave out filler, slogans, and stacked abstractions. Do not dress up a simple decision so it sounds more important than it is. If a sentence only restates the one before it, cut it.
